---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout
  title="Sierra Leone: DecoPlastic"
  description="DecoPlastic Sierra Leone establishes a locally rooted system for plastic collection, sorting, processing and manufacturing, led by Sierra Leone Engineering Solutions."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow reveal"><a href={base} style="color:inherit;">&larr; Plastic Circle West Africa</a></p>
      <h1 class="reveal">DecoPlastic, Sierra Leone</h1>
      <p class="lede reveal">
        A locally rooted circular economy model that converts unmanaged
        plastic waste in Sierra Leone into marketable products, jobs and
        longer-term local productive capacity.
      </p>

      <div class="stat-bar">
        <div class="stat">
          <p class="stat-label">Plastic waste generated</p>
          <p class="stat-value">~130,000 t / year</p>
          <p class="stat-note">only around 7,200 tonnes properly recycled domestically (World Bank, 2024)</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <p class="stat-label">Freetown collection</p>
          <p class="stat-value">46% of households</p>
          <p class="stat-note">served by waste collection; only 25% of city waste reaches dumpsites (World Bank, 2021)</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <p class="stat-label">Uncollected daily</p>
          <p class="stat-value">300+ tonnes / day</p>
          <p class="stat-note">buried, burned or dumped in waterways and drains in Freetown</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Local context</p>
        <h2>Why Sierra Leone, why now</h2>
        <p>
          Sierra Leone generates an estimated 130,000 tonnes of plastic waste
          a year, while domestic recycling capacity remains far below
          national need. In Freetown, more than half of households are not
          served by formal waste collection, and blocked drains intensify
          flooding and public-health risk. A peer-reviewed beach-litter study
          documented plastic as the dominant litter category on Sierra
          Leone's coastline, accounting for around 70% of litter by count,
          led by plastic bottles, water sachets, and caps and lids (Lavelle
          et al., 2024).
        </p>
        <p>
          At the same time, Sierra Leone has adopted a National Plastic and
          Plastic Waste Policy, and Freetown is one of five cities in UNDP
          and GEF's Shifting to Zero Waste Against Pollution (SWAP)
          programme, giving DecoPlastic a direct policy anchor to align
          with.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section panel wine" style="margin: 0 clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 2.5rem); width:auto; padding: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem) clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem);">
    <p class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--blush);">Lead implementation partner</p>
    <h2>Sierra Leone Engineering Solutions</h2>
    <p style="max-width: 680px;">
      Sierra Leone Engineering Solutions (C.S.O.), led by <strong>Ishmael Faye</strong>,
      is the local implementation lead for DecoPlastic: operational
      coordination, local stakeholder engagement, community mobilisation and
      sourcing relationships on the ground in Sierra Leone. It works
      alongside Ayara Foundation Switzerland, which leads strategy,
      technical direction, governance, fundraising and international
      partnerships, and Aquitas (Switzerland) Ltd., which provides
      independent monitoring, evaluation, accountability and learning (MEAL).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Approach</p>
        <h2>From collection to local manufacturing</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid reveal">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Recover</h3>
          <p>
            Neighbourhood-based collectors, local aggregators, women's and
            youth groups and institutional drop-off partners such as
            schools, hospitality actors and businesses feed a structured
            sourcing model, organising rather than displacing existing
            informal recovery.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Prepare</h3>
          <p>
            Plastic is sorted by resin type, colour and quality against a
            resin-based acceptance matrix, cleaned and prepared for
            production, with roughly 60&ndash;75% of collected material
            expected to enter productive use.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Make</h3>
          <p>
            Technology transferred through the ECOLLABO8 partnership &mdash;
            moulded products, sheet press, flow moulding extrusion and
            extrusion press &mdash; converts recovered plastic into
            furniture, outdoor products, surface materials, household items
            and bespoke solutions for schools, hospitality and offices.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Sell &amp; reinvest</h3>
          <p>
            Revenue comes from product sales, bespoke institutional orders,
            and collection and recovery service contracts, with surpluses
            reinvested into jobs, maintenance and gradual expansion.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Operational resilience</p>
        <h2>Built for Sierra Leone's conditions</h2>
        <p>
          Sierra Leone's business environment remains constrained by
          frequent power outages, with around 62% of firms owning or sharing
          a generator. DecoPlastic integrates a hybrid solar, battery and
          generator energy system from the outset, protecting production
          continuity and equipment rather than treating energy resilience as
          an optional add-on.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Partners</p>
        <h2>Delivered together</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid reveal">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Ayara Foundation Switzerland</h3>
          <p>Programme lead: strategy, technical direction, governance, fundraising and international partnerships.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Sierra Leone Engineering Solutions</h3>
          <p>Local implementation lead: community engagement, operational coordination and sourcing relationships, led by Ishmael Faye.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>ECOLLABO8</h3>
          <p>Technology partner: recycling machinery, technical onboarding, production know-how and training.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Aquitas (Switzerland)</h3>
          <p>Independent MEAL and evidence partner: baselines, indicators, data quality and outcome monitoring.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section panel wine" style="margin: 0 clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 2.5rem) clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem); width:auto; padding: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem) clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem); text-align:center;">
    <h2>Support DecoPlastic Sierra Leone</h2>
    <p style="max-width:560px; margin: 0 auto 1.5em;">
      Ayara Foundation Switzerland is seeking grant, co-funding and strategic
      partners for DecoPlastic, including full-site and component financing.
    </p>
    <a class="pill-btn outline on-dark" href={`${base}contact`}>Get in Touch</a>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .pill-btn.outline.on-dark {
    border-color: var(--blush);
    color: var(--blush-pale);
  }

  .pill-btn.outline.on-dark:hover {
    background: var(--blush-pale);
    color: var(--wine-dark);
  }
</style>
